+
+## Client-side view cache (keep-alive)
+
+Navigation uses Astro's `<ClientRouter />`. By default it replaces the whole
+`<body>` on every navigation, so going back to a page you already visited
+refetches, re-parses, re-renders and re-hydrates it from scratch.
+
+`src/scripts/view-cache.ts` keeps recently visited views alive instead:
+
+- When you navigate away, the page's `<main data-view-root>` is moved into a
+  hidden `[data-view-cache-store]` container at the end of `<body>`. The store is
+  `transition:persist`ed, so the parked DOM never leaves the document and its
+  React islands keep their state.
+- When you navigate to a URL whose view is parked, the network request is
+  skipped and the parked element is moved back into place (title and any
+  page-specific head styles are restored too).
+
+Details:
+
+- Up to 10 views are kept (LRU) for at most 10 minutes.
+- Form submissions always hit the server and drop the target's cached view.
+- Opt a page out with `<Layout keepAlive={false}>`.
+- `window.viewCache` exposes `has(url)`, `invalidate(url?)`, `clear()`, `keys()`
+  and `size`; `view-cache:park` / `view-cache:restore` events fire on `document`.
